# Canonical deploy integrity lock

## Permanent policy

Production artifacts are published only from the **single canonical working tree** of each repository, at a committed revision that matches `origin/<branch>`.

## Mandatory controls

1. **Clean tree** — `git status --porcelain` empty
2. **Origin sync** — `HEAD == origin/<branch>`
3. **Exclusive publish lock** — atomic `mkdir` on `.git/onecab-canonical-publish.lockdir` for the whole bundle/publish window
4. **Freeze** — deploy-relevant paths are `chmod a-w` while bundling so concurrent edits cannot enter the artifact
5. **Revision pin** — record and re-verify `HEAD` before and after publish

## Entry points

| Surface | Script |
| --- | --- |
| Edge functions | `scripts/deploy-edge-clean-preflight.sh` |
| Admin web | `scripts/publish-admin-web-clean-preflight.sh` |
| Customer OTA | `onecab-customer-native/scripts/publish-production-ota.sh` |
| Driver OTA | `onecab-driver-native/scripts/publish-production-ota.sh` |
| Corporate/Guest web | `onecab-central-hub/scripts/publish-web-clean-preflight.sh` then Lovable Publish |
| Premium/Admin portal | `onecab-premium-build/scripts/publish-web-clean-preflight.sh` then Lovable Publish |

## Forbidden

- Deploy/OTA from dirty or intermediate trees
- Parallel edit + deploy of the same tree without the publish lock
- Competing working trees / worktrees for production artifacts
- Claiming version-counter bumps equal a new binary (verify `ezbr_sha256` / OTA group)

Shared helper: `scripts/lib/canonical-tree-publish-guard.sh`
